    "body": "This post explores a hypothetical scenario comparing Q4 and Q8 quantization levels for local LLMs. The objective is to understand the potential trade-offs between memory usage and accuracy, based on synthetic experimental data. \n\nIn this hypothetical setup, a Q4 configuration is estimated to require 6 GB of VRAM, while a Q8 configuration would need 10 GB. This represents a significant difference in memory footprint. To assess accuracy, a hypothetical 20-question check was devised. The Q4 model hypothetically answered 14 questions correctly, whereas the Q8 model hypothetically achieved 16 correct answers. Crucially, the hardware and prompts used were identical across both hypothetical configurations (F3). \n\nIt is important to emphasize that this is a purely hypothetical comparison. No actual benchmark or statistical significance test was performed (F4). The VRAM figures and accuracy scores are synthetic experimental inputs (F1, F2) and should not be treated as measured results or personal experience. The goal is to initiate a discussion on how such trade-offs might manifest in practice.",
