    "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical experiment designed to investigate the relationship between quantization levels (Q4 and Q8) and their potential impact on VRAM usage and accuracy in local LLMs. The scenario is purely illustrative and based on synthetic inputs.\n\nAccording to the hypothetical data, a Q4 model is projected to consume 6 GB of VRAM, compared to 10 GB for a Q8 model (F1). This suggests a substantial difference in memory requirements. In terms of hypothetical performance, a 20-question assessment yielded 14 correct answers for Q4 and 16 for Q8 (F2). The experimental conditions, including hardware and prompts, were kept identical throughout this hypothetical comparison (F3).\n\nIt must be stressed that these figures are derived from a hypothetical setup and do not represent real-world measurements or benchmarks (F4). No actual tests were conducted. This exploration aims to stimulate a technical discussion about the theoretical implications of choosing different quantization levels, considering both resource constraints and potential accuracy gains, while strictly adhering to the hypothetical nature of the data.",
